      "name": "Lois Frankel",
      "party": "Democratic",
      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Lois Frankel has served as U.S. Representative for Florida's 22nd Congressional District since 2013 and shifted her candidacy to the new 23rd District after redistricting. She previously served as Mayor of West Palm Beach (2003-2011) and in the Florida House of Representatives (1986-1992, 1994-2002), including as Minority Leader. Frankel holds a B.A. from Boston University and a J.D. from Georgetown University Law Center.",
